# What the knowledge graph should not index.
#
# Everything below is GENERATED from somewhere else in this repo. Indexing it
# doubles the graph with copies of files that already have nodes, and makes
# "what calls X?" answer with a build artefact instead of the source.
#
# graphify falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, but these are
# declared in nested per-package .gitignore files, so they are spelled out here.

# @viliha/vui-core: a literal copy of packages/ui/src, compiled.
packages/core/src/
packages/core/dist/

# @viliha/vui-theme: generated from packages/ui/src/theme.css.
packages/theme/theme.css
packages/theme/dist/

# @viliha/vui-vue: compiled SFCs.
packages/vue/dist/

# The scaffold `vui init` copies: a snapshot of apps/backoffice, so every file
# in it is a duplicate of one that is already indexed.
packages/ui/template/

# The docs-site snapshot the MCP server serves: generated from apps/backoffice/out.
packages/ui/docs/

# Build output and lockfiles.
apps/*/out/
apps/*/.next/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Brand assets and screenshots. Each image costs its own vision agent to extract,
# and "this is the logo" is not a fact the graph needs to answer a question about
# how the code works. Add a diagram here only if it explains architecture.
*.png
*.svg
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.ico
